WEBVTT

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:17.270
Lord Bashbarza!

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:18.900
You look as awesome as ever today!

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.040
Yes, I know.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.290
The greatest genius in the whole academy.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.680
I do tire of hearing that.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.250
Perhaps I should teach it a different phrase.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.240
Bashbarza?

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.010
I have something to tell...

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.660
What is this?

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.670
Do not enter without permission.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:41.890
Do not enter!

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.960
Does it interest you?

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.070
Then I suppose I have no choice! 
I shall make an exception and tell you!

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:52.720
I am in the midst of creating 
a compressed magic weapon.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:53.530
I see.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.600
Using mythril, with its high magic 
absorption rate, as the main material,

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.200
a number of magical elements are combined.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.300
Though continued compression,

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.210
magical energy hundreds of times stronger 
than it was originally is stored...

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.170
to create a mega-bomb!

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:18.560
With this, I shall reign as the greatest 
of any of the Four Generals in history!

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:23.070
But doesn't this need a 
tremendous amount of mythril?

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:24.160
It isn't a problem.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.190
I'm having it delivered at 
four times the old pace.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.690
I hear that they're having trouble on site.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.410
That's what makes it perfect.

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:33.650
That mine retains traces 
of Dariel's contributions.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.200
It makes you want to torment 
them for no reason, doesn't it?

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.580
That's actually what brings me here.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.080
The Mythril Mine has been stolen from us.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:47.240
Huh?

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:52.290
They say the humans are already 
in full possession of it.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:53.910
Th...

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.050
That can't be!

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:59.750
The situation is even more grave than that.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:02.560
Someone wants to lodge a complaint with you.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:05.020
A-And who would that be?

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.200
Who <i>dares</i> to rebuke me?

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.280
I'll drive them out of the Demon King's Army!

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:11.610
It's the Demon King himself.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:12.840
Wha?!

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:32.710
<b>Chillin'</b>

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:32.710
<b>in My 30s after Getting Fired from the Demon King's Army</b>

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:47.030
<b>Episode 4</b>

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:47.030
<b>Dariel Negotiates.</b>

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.440
You know...

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:54.740
I really love a festival.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.510
Admiring the pretty flowers...

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:59.380
while eating yummy food and drinking alcohol!

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.460
And I have the court ladies 
dress up all pretty, too!

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.390
In accessories made of mythril, you know?

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.810
By the way...

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.850
I've heard that the all-important 
mythril is gone.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.010
What is the meaning of that?

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.150
I told you so many times.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.570
Why didn't you stop trying to make that bomb?

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:25.340
The portion... allotted for a-accessories...

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.570
was in... the additional order...

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:30.390
The one for four times the normal amount?

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.490
That's asking for the impossible,
 don'tcha think?

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:38.570
The accessories thing was 
all just pretext anyway.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.250
What?

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.920
It was to get you to stop 
trying to make that bomb.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:47.680
I was trying to be nice so that 
your pride wouldn't get wounded.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:53.680
But you are so much dumber 
than I thought you were.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:58.520
You have made an epic mistake 
of unparalleled proportions.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.030
You need to make this right.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.280
Right here, right now.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.820
Now, say you're sorry.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:10.780
What?

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:14.150
When you mess up, you're supposed
 to say you're sorry, right?

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.820
B-But this was all because the Knockers...

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.170
Say you're sorry!

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:29.240
I... I...

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:32.470
I-I...

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.350
I am...

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.800
very...very sorry.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:42.780
The idiot has gotten just 
a teensy bit smarter.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:47.850
Ya know, you should have 
him help you out more.

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:51.910
Let's see...what was his name again?

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:54.520
Oh, Dariel!

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:58.210
Now, he's what you'd call gifted.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.880
He's smart and kind.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.850
And the reason your papa served so 
well as one of the Four Generals...

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:09.280
was because he kept soldiers like 
my Dariel close to him!

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:14.350
If you understand now, then you can go.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:18.020
Make sure you reflect on yourself lots 
at home before you come back, 'kay?

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:26.030
Now, what will you do?

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:29.830
After all, Dariel isn't here anymore.

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:40.870
<i>He called me stupid </i>twice<i>!</i>

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:42.460
<i>And...</i>

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.880
<i>even His Majesty the Demon King...</i>

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.430
<i>said that guy's name!</i>

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:00.110
Mister Dariel...

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:06.000
This is the first time I've seen 
Lux Village so lively and bustling.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.130
Different kinds of people will start 
coming here, and it will get even busier.

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:11.160
That's something...

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:16.260
we'd want to show our children as 
soon as possible, don't you think?

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:24.840
Oh, but please don't worry.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:30.840
Even if I have children, I'll be 
sure to treasure my husband as well.

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:32.840
<i>Why is she saying that to me?</i>

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:35.740
Th-That's a lovely notion.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:37.310
L-Lovely?

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:42.190
M-Mister Dariel, I just know 
you'll make a lovely father, too!

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.690
S-S-So...

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.590
will you be my f-f-f...

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.600
f-f-fian...

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:50.530
Fight!

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:55.160
Hey you! How dare you 
talk about us like that!

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:58.340
Sorry, Malika. I'm going to go over there.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:07:59.310
Oh...

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:01.660
Tonight is the Great Feast,

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:04.470
so, please... come home early...

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:06.170
won't you?

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:10.840
<i>I feel like she was about 
to say something terrifying.</i>

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:13.580
<i>No. I'm sure I'm just imagining it.</i>

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:16.350
Who d'you think you are?

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.340
Stop right there.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.600
Big Bro!

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:24.540
But he was saying that adventurers 
from the countryside are fakes!

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:26.160
Pardon us.

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:30.280
I am leading a group of adventurers 
dispatched from Campbell Town.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:31.940
My name is Fittbitan.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.430
H-Hello.

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:37.660
I had heard that this village 
had only two adventurers.

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:39.490
Could it be that you...

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:42.540
Oh. Yes, though I'm just a novice.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.290
D-rank?

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:48.790
I suppose the rumors are just that, then.

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:52.000
I'd heard that the the two of you 
had recaptured the Mythril Mine.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.980
What sort of sleight of hand did you use?

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:56.060
We were lucky, that's all.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:58.800
Must have been. You're D-rank, after all.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.540
You little...

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:01.180
Don't.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:03.230
But that guy is talking about you!

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:06.060
We will take over all work 
relating to the mine.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:08.930
You two can return to doing your odd jobs.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:09.770
And...

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:15.030
Keep that disrespectful youngster 
there on a tight leash.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:17.530
Speaking of Campbell Town...

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.320
you were the ones who went after 
the blaze deathscythe, weren't you?

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:23.660
You know about that?

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:25.910
Well, it did come to our area.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:28.700
According to what I heard,

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:34.000
the adventurers of Campbell Town tried to 
corner the blaze deathscythe and failed.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.590
And the area it escaped to was Lux Village.

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:40.830
The blaze deathscythe which 
you allowed to escape was

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:42.220
first spotted again by this man.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:45.060
He doesn't need a leash.

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:47.180
Big Bro!

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:49.060
Let's go, Gashita.

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:51.850
That's right!

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:55.070
The one who took down that 
stupid snake was my big bro!

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:57.590
He's the one who cleaned up your mess!

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:59.740
You should at least say thanks!

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.400
<i>Th-This is bad!</i>

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.760
<i>I ended up picking a fight with them!</i>

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:08.920
Th-The blaze deathscythe... 
You say you defeated it?

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.480
I'd heard some rumors, but...

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:11.480
That's incredible!

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:14.300
A single adventurer from 
Lux Village hunted it down?

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.550
Huh? Oh, um...

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:16.550
I can't believe it!

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:19.040
Yes, I did manage that somehow.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:20.890
I did think I might die, though.

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:22.410
Incredible!

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:23.310
He killed it in a one-on-one fight?

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:23.930
That's an A-rank deed!

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:23.930
For real?

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:23.930
Wow!

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:26.430
He's an A-rank adventurer! An A-rank!

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:26.430
Huh? Oh! Just... Wait!

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:34.230
Hip, hip, hooray! Hip, hip, hooray!

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.010
<i>I learned after I got home...</i>

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:34.230
<i>that the ones who made the 
mistake during the mission...</i>

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:37.070
<i>were in Fittbitan's party.</i>

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:40.070
<b>Chillin'
 in My 30s after Getting Fired from the Demon King's Army</b>

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.080
What does that mean, Gashita?

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.840
I told you already!

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:49.040
That adventurer named Fittbitan...

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:51.820
was talking trash about my big bro!

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:55.770
I shall end him.

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:57.380
<i>That's just like she was 
when she killed the deer!</i>

00:10:57.380 --> 00:11:00.210
Anyone who dares act discourteously 
toward Mister Dariel...

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:02.160
shall pay for it with their life.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.170
Get his ass, Malika!

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:05.640
Stop that, Gashita!

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.390
Now, let's calm down.

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:10.510
I can understand how they feel.

00:11:10.510 --> 00:11:16.430
It may surprise you, but adventurers only 
have ranks to prove their worth.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.860
That has nothing to do with this!

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:23.800
To hurt Mister Dariel, my husband...

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:25.370
I'll never forgive them!

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:26.370
What?

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:27.200
Oh!

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:28.930
N-No, it's not like that!

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:32.140
Wh-When I said "husband" 
I meant in the future.

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:34.480
I-I have to go check on the food!

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:36.460
<i>H-Husband?</i>

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:41.120
Big Bro! C'mon, drink with me!

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:43.030
Oh, right. Guild Master!

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:45.020
How's the revival of the 
village comin' along?

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:46.220
Oh, that's right!

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.100
Wasn't that the purpose of this gathering?

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:50.850
It's not good.

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:53.700
Is that so, sir?

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.190
Sir?!

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:55.930
<i>Not in that sense...</i>

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:58.210
Take good care of my daughter, son!

00:11:58.210 --> 00:11:59.860
<i>That's not where I was going with this!</i>

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.860
Wow! Congratulations! What happy news!

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:01.860
No, I didn't mean...

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:04.050
Stop that right now!

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:06.370
Everyone, let's discuss the revival of the...

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:10.330
The one who's gonna marry my big bro is me!

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:12.570
Yeah!

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.580
<i>This is a complete mess.</i>

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:19.000
Did you say negotiations with the Knockers...

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:20.760
Mister Bestfred?

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:22.920
Yes.

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:27.180
I came from Center Guild to speak with them,

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.930
but they are wary of me for some reason.

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:33.440
They've said they won't agree 
to anyone's words but yours.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:36.940
The Knockers were tyrannized by the demons...

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:40.710
so it may be difficult for them 
to trust any outsiders right now.

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:44.800
Then, I wonder why yours are
 the only words they trust?

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:46.410
Well...

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:51.410
They seem to feel that I saved 
them from the rule of the demons.

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:53.360
I see.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:56.200
Then, for the negotiations 
to proceed smoothly,

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:58.270
will you act as an intermediary for us?

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:03.220
If the negotiations end in failure...

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.510
What will happen to them?

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:09.100
The cooperation of the Knockers 
is absolutely essential!

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.090
But we don't want to force them.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:13.100
That is why we hope for your assistance.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:17.850
All right.

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:24.660
You must all be feeling nervous,

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:27.580
but won't you please hear what he has to say?

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.870
All righty!

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.000
Wha?!

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.000
We'll listen to everything he has to say!

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:38.080
Thank you so much!

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:40.400
I will be able to handle 
the rest myself, so...

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:41.400
Of course.

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:43.960
<i>And suddenly I have nothing to do.</i>

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:45.880
<i>Maybe I'll head home.</i>

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:46.590
Oh!

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:48.770
It's the A-rank guy!

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:51.180
Shh! Don't talk to him!

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:52.700
Hello.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:56.180
I-I heard that management came 
to ask for you in person.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.940
Yes. What about all of you?

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:01.600
As you can see, we're on a bodyguard quest.

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:04.180
We won't let a single 
one of them get past us.

00:14:04.180 --> 00:14:06.000
<i>Knockers, my friends!</i>

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.950
<i>Please, come home to us.</i>

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:12.080
<i>His Majesty the Demon King has forgiven you.</i>

00:14:10.970 --> 00:14:12.080
<i>This voice...</i>

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:15.250
I have to... use the bathroom!

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:16.890
Wow!

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:18.250
He must <i>really</i> need to use the bathroom.

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:20.540
<i>Lately, I've realized...</i>

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:24.140
<i>that if I wrap myself in Aura instead 
of sending it into my weapons,</i>

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:25.800
<i>I can run faster.</i>

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:30.840
<i>There aren't many soldiers.</i>

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:32.300
A human?

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:34.350
What are you doing?

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:36.100
It's an enemy adventurer!

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:42.620
Withdraw, adventurer!

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:44.480
We have no intention of fighting.

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:46.490
Fall back now, while we can.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:47.490
Sir!

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:50.740
Rizet, it's me!

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:51.780
What?

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:54.210
D... D...

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:57.160
Dariel!

00:14:57.940 --> 00:15:00.290
I was so worried about you!

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:03.580
Everything's been such a mess since you left!

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:06.090
<i>That's right.</i>

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:08.690
<i>This is what a hug is supposed to feel like.</i>

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:17.190
What have you been doing all this time?

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:18.430
Tell me everything.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:21.440
<i>He says to tell him everything, but...</i>

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:25.750
I-Is it because of back then?

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:26.440
Huh?

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:30.830
Because on the day you were fired, 
I said those mean things to you?

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:32.140
What?

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:32.980
You have it wrong!

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:34.770
I didn't say those things because I hate you!

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:36.860
You know I didn't actually mean
any of that, right?

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:37.450
After all...

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:40.000
you're my...

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:42.210
my...

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:43.730
<i>This guy.</i>

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:46.170
<i>He's always let things get to him too much.</i>

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:47.690
<i>I guess I have no choice.</i>

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:49.970
I know.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:52.050
Rizet, it isn't your fault.

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:54.180
I...

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:58.520
The truth is, I'm a human.

00:15:59.160 --> 00:15:59.770
What?

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:05.800
Really?

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:08.800
Keep it just between us, all right?

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:09.950
All right.

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:12.490
So... what happened to bring you here?

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:14.640
What happened? Well...

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:15.740
It's all your fault.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.320
Me?

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:20.500
Day-to-day operations in the Demon
 King's Army are just horrible right now.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.910
When you were acting as 
an assistant, it was different.

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:27.510
You'd take that idiot son's unreasonable 
orders and relay them in a milder form.

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:30.210
And you provided as much back up to everyone 
in the field as you could.

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:32.140
But...

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:36.210
Having lost all that, the chain of command
 is on the verge of collapse.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:39.390
Right now, everyone in the army,
 from top to bottom, is mad about something.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:42.310
The final blow was a reprimand 
from His Majesty the Demon King.

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:46.600
That idiot son's been taking his anger out
on everyone he meets ever since.

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:48.150
<i>"Idiot son"?</i>

00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:52.450
We've been ordered to keep
our hands off the mine.

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:54.490
Then why are you here?

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:57.950
I have permission from his 
majesty the Demon King.

00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:01.700
I need to properly reconcile with the 
Knockers and resolve any grievances.

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:05.040
We must show the other demi-humans 
that we can do this.

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:09.540
They are the precious foundation 
of the Demon King's Army.

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:12.460
<i>This guy really is an earnest one.</i>

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:14.960
Say, Dariel.

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:15.760
Yeah?

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:18.650
Why don't you come back 
to the Demon King's Army?

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:21.580
Don't ask the impossible. 
I told you, I'm human.

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.230
If I keep quiet about it, it's fine!

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.900
The top officers fired me.

00:17:27.930 --> 00:17:31.440
And among those top officers, 
there is someone who wants you back.

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:32.690
What?

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:35.050
Lady Doroye.

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:37.440
She's been looking for you this whole time.

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:41.460
Dariel, even if we're from different races...

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:43.550
you're my friend!

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:45.870
So, come back to us!

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:49.380
I'm sorry, Rizet.

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:52.630
I'm happy you feel that way...

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:58.030
but when I was fired and didn't know 
what to do, some people took me in.

00:17:58.030 --> 00:18:01.100
Right now, I want to work for their sakes.

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:08.350
I'm sorry, but I'm taking you back even 
if I have to render you unconscious.

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:10.520
You are needed!

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.440
I can't go back...

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:18.200
but I've thought up a good idea.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:21.740
Would you guys like to buy some mythril?

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:24.240
What?

00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:30.980
Sell mythril to the demons?!

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:32.750
Are you in earnest, Mister Dariel?

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:34.400
Yes.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:38.010
Which is why I had a representative 
of the demons come here.

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:42.490
But this is our turn to monopolize 
the mythril, isn't it?

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:43.990
Exactly.

00:18:43.990 --> 00:18:47.480
For the demons, the mythril 
shortage is a grave problem.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:51.760
That is precisely why they 
will come to take it back.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:54.770
And humans will, of course, 
respond to their attack.

00:18:55.090 --> 00:18:56.860
If both sides clash...

00:18:57.420 --> 00:18:59.510
it will become a gruesome battle.

00:18:59.510 --> 00:19:02.250
That would be the worst case for both sides.

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:07.020
But if they were able to maintain a supply,

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:09.010
the Demon King's Army would not attack.

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:09.670
Still...

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:12.170
I have no intention of giving up
our advantage here.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:14.130
which is why setting the negotiated price...

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:17.630
at four times market value seems appropriate.

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:20.230
That seems too...

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:21.630
We demons...

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:25.280
would like to replenish our 
mythril as soon as possible.

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:27.560
Even if we fought, that would not 
absolutely guarantee such an outcome.

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:31.770
As such, we are not unwilling 
to solve the problem with money.

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:34.600
Just a moment, please.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:37.680
I am against this.

00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:40.560
Asking us to sell you mythril 
because you've lost access to it...

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:42.140
Now, that's brazen.

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:45.910
Talking things out with the 
demons after all this time...

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:49.000
Impossible!

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:55.080
That's why we must.

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.840
Mythril is trivial...

00:19:58.310 --> 00:20:01.840
and now no one's blood will 
ever be shed for it again!

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:03.490
That is why we will talk!

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:09.950
Such arrogance from a mere D-rank...

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:14.160
My lord Bestfred, these 
negotiations are meaningless.

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:15.360
Why?

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:17.150
Well, because...

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:21.600
When I ask "why," that is 
not what I am asking about.

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:24.030
The services I've requested of you 
are security and escort. That is all.

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:26.590
You are the brazen one here.

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:30.290
Advice on political matters 
is not a part of your quest.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:34.270
Let's return to our discussion, Mister Dariel.

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:38.150
This demon is someone we can trust.

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:39.210
That's why I had him come here...

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:41.460
all alone...

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:43.020
risking his life.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:47.970
Honored demon guest,

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:50.510
we shall share our mythril with you.

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:58.650
Then, as to the details of 
the transaction, first...

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:06.670
Thanks to you, I was able to 
apologize to the Knockers, too.

00:21:06.670 --> 00:21:08.370
Thank you for everything, Dariel.

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:10.280
No, thank you.

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:13.000
If you hadn't been here, I wouldn't have 
been able to make a bargain like this.

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:17.060
Both are precious to me.

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:19.900
You mean both demons and humans?

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:20.420
Yes.

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:24.960
If Lord Granbarza hadn't taken
 me in when I was a baby,

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:27.380
I would have died long ago.

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:30.250
At some point, race has ceased to matter.

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:32.960
It would be nice if everyone 
could be friends, wouldn't it?

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:33.900
That it would.

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:09.490
You mean... a smithy?

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:12.970
Yes. We'd like for you to 
build a mythril workshop.

00:23:13.470 --> 00:23:16.460
<i>I've heard that there was one 
in this village long ago.</i>

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:21.670
<i>So, he wants me to find it and revive it?</i>

00:23:22.560 --> 00:23:24.320
<i>Could this be it?</i>

00:23:28.490 --> 00:23:30.670
Master smiths of Campbell Town!

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:32.930
Keep your hands moving!

00:23:36.590 --> 00:23:39.730
<i>A-Are they... already doing something here?</i>

00:23:41.640 --> 00:23:46.270
Next time on <i>Chillin' in My 30s After 
Getting Fired from the Demon King's Army</i>...

00:23:46.270 --> 00:23:48.530
"Dariel Fights in a Duel."

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:51.070
<b>Episode 5</b>

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:51.070
<b>Dariel Fights in a Duel.</b>
